  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, a preference for a lottery that is more left-skewed (i.e., more probability mass on favorable outcomes). However, the individual in the verbal report only considers the probability of winning (positive outcome), not the distribution of those outcomes or the skewness. The report does not reference the structure of the outcomes (e.g., 4000€ vs. 2000€ vs. 0€), nor does it compare the concentration of probability on favorable outcomes. The individual’s justification is about the chance of winning (50% vs. 25%), which is a different concept. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The information considered (probability of winning) is not equivalent to the information required for skewness analysis. The justification also does not reflect the rule of preferring more left-skewed lotteries. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
